  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened occupational safety and health framework and protection of workers in high-risk sectors in line with international labour standards and EU directives</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILO supports Ukraine in strengthening the protection of workers against heightened occupational safety and health (OSH) risks, particularly in frontline regions and critical sectors such as energy. In the context of the Russian Federation&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122;s military aggression against Ukraine, many worksites remain exposed to severe physical and psychosocial hazards. 
At sector and enterprise levels, the ILO supports the development of OSH protocols tailored to wartime and high-risk conditions, including mine and UXO safety procedures, emergency preparedness and monitoring mechanisms, and promotes workplace-based psychosocial services to address trauma, fatigue and stress. These measures contribute to safer working conditions and improved protection of workers during recovery and reconstruction.
In parallel, the intervention assists tripartite constituents in updating the OSH legislative and regulatory framework in line with international labour standards and EU directives, including advancing the ratification and implementation of the Promotional Framework for Occupational Safety and Health Convention, 2006 (No. 187), and the Biological Hazards in the Working Environment Convention, 2025 (No. 192).</narrative>
  </description>
